        The record's own title "Ettepanek" happens to be publishable, but a
        public title is given explicitly anyway, which is the safer practice:
        an application then never has to decide whether RecordMetadata/RecordTitle
        may be shown to someone without access to the restricted content. This
        also matters after the restriction period expires, when the record has to
        be published and a title prepared in advance is available.
      -->
