      <PublicRecordAbstract>Ettepanek uue lahenduse kasutuselevõtuks.</PublicRecordAbstract>
      <!--
        File Ettepanek.txt is restricted as a whole: its Access is "AK", never
        more permissive than the document-level Access above it. An application
        that understands file-level access but cannot segment the file therefore
        withholds the whole file, which is safe.

        An application that recognises the SegmentationMethod value may go
        further. This file is plain text, so "plaintext-blocks-v1" applies: a
        paragraph is a run of non-blank lines, words are counted over the whole
        file, and page ranges must not be used. Before applying any range, the
        application segments the file itself and checks that it arrives at the
        same totals as SegmentationCheck — 12 paragraphs and 287 words, the two
        counts plaintext-blocks-v1 requires. If either differs, the two
        implementations do not in fact segment this file alike, every range
        below is therefore suspect, and the application keeps the whole file
        restricted instead of publishing a span next to the restricted one.
        DefaultPartAccessConditionsCode
        says that any part of this file not covered by an AccessGroup below is in
        fact "Avalik", so only the restricted islands need to be enumerated —
        there is no need to list every public paragraph. Those islands are
        paragraphs 3-4 and a single word elsewhere in the file (word 42, e.g. a
        personal identification code mentioned in passing in an otherwise public
        paragraph). Since they carry the identical access condition and
        restriction, they are listed together under one AccessGroup, so the
        Access/AccessRestriction data only needs to be written once instead of
        being repeated per range. Note that the word range is independent of the
        paragraph range and does not require the paragraph containing it to be
        listed. Word and paragraph numbering both follow SegmentationMethod.
      -->
