        permits PageRange only, forbidding paragraph and word ranges. Page
        granularity is enough to withhold the two scanned pages that bear
        restricted content while releasing the rest.

        SegmentationCheck gives the only count pdf-pages-v1 requires: the total
        number of pages, 11. A receiver that traverses the PDF page tree and
        arrives at a different number has understood the file's page structure
        differently from the sender — the usual cause being a page tree walked
        in another order or nested page groups counted wrongly — so the page
        numbers below would not mean the same thing to both parties, and the
        file stays fully restricted.

        Note that the page numbers are positions in the file, not the numbers
        printed on the scanned originals, which for a scanned volume often start
        somewhere else entirely. Note also that pdf-pages-v1 covers page content
        only: if this PDF carried restricted information in its metadata,
        bookmarks or an embedded file, page ranges would not be enough and the
        file would have to stay fully restricted.

        DefaultPartAccessConditionsCode is "Avalik", so the pages not listed below
        are public. Pages 4-5 are restricted on a different legal basis
        (business secret) than the rest of the record, with its own shorter
        expiry date, which shows why each AccessGroup carries a complete
        AccessRestriction of its own rather than inheriting one.
